  "rationales": {"U":"'three-phase clocks must be clocked simultaneously 602 times' lacks context for non-hardware readers; 'clocked' is domain-specific jargon without definition, and 'simultaneously' falsely implies zero skew across physically separate sections — impairing Understandability for cross-functional stakeholders.", "A":"'simultaneously' is physically impossible across distributed sections; 'Image Section and Store Section three-phase clocks' ambiguously assigns ownership — does each section have its own three-phase clock? Or is there one shared clock with three phases? The phrase 'clocked simultaneously 602 times' conflates event count with timing coordination, violating Unambiguity.", "C":"The requirement may be technically plausible in a synchronous ASIC design, but correctness cannot be assessed without knowing clock topology, reset behavior, or whether 602 is derived from image width/depth — no evidence of validation source or derivation, so score reflects medium confidence in intent alignment.", "V":"No observable pass/fail criterion: 'must be clocked simultaneously 602 times' provides no measurable signal (e.g., 'within ±1 ns skew', 'with no missed edges', or 'verified via logic analyzer trace capturing CLK_A_phase1, CLK_B_phase1...') — thus fundamentally unverifiable in test or review."}, 
  "suggestions": {"U":"The Image Section and the Store Section each contain a three-phase clock generator; to transfer one image, both generators shall advance through exactly 602 full three-phase cycles, with phase-aligned rising edges on all six clock signals (three per section).", "A":"The Image Section clock generator and the Store Section clock generator shall each produce three non-overlapping clock phases (P1, P2, P3); for one image transfer, both generators shall complete exactly 602 full phase cycles, where each cycle consists of one assertion of P1, one of P2, and one of P3 in sequence; the rising edge of P1 in the Image Section shall occur within 5 ns of the rising edge of P1 in the Store Section for all 602 cycles.", "C":"Keep as-is pending verification against hardware specification §4.2.1 and image buffer depth calculation; if 602 derives from 100.333... pixels, revise to integer-aligned value.", "V":"For each image transfer, a logic analyzer shall capture all six clock signals (Image_P1, Image_P2, Image_P3, Store_P1, Store_P2, Store_P3) at ≥1 GS/s; analysis shall confirm: (a) exactly 602 rising edges on Image_P1 and Store_P1; (b) |t(Image_P1_n) − t(Store_P1_n)| ≤ 5 ns for n = 1 to 602; (c) no missing or extra P1–P3 transitions per cycle."}, 
